+# Findings
+
+I would not sign off on this vault for mainnet deposits as it stands today.
+
+The existing `forge test` suite is green, but it only proves the vault works against standard ERC20 mocks and a simplified Aave mock. The new tests I added under `test/` exercise properties the current suite does not: a pinned mainnet fork against real USDT/Aave, custody/accounting conservation, and fuzzed fee bounds.
+
+No files under `src/`, `test/UsdtYieldVault.t.sol`, or `test/mocks/` were changed.
+
+## 1. Critical: deposits revert against real mainnet USDT
+
+`UsdtYieldVault.deposit()` calls:
+
+```solidity
+usdt.approve(address(aavePool), amount);
+```
+
+That is a high-level `IERC20.approve` call, so Solidity expects a `bool` return value. Mainnet USDT's `approve` returns no data. On the fork, USDT emits the `Approval` event and returns with no data, then the vault reverts while decoding the missing `bool`. This means the first real deposit into the mainnet vault cannot complete.
+
+How I found it: `test/UsdtYieldVaultMainnetFork.t.sol`, pinned at block `26026384`, using:
+
+- USDT: `0xdAC17F958D2ee523a2206206994597C13D831ec7`
+- Aave V3 Pool: `0x87870Bca3F3fD6335C3F4ce8392D69350B4fA4E2`
+- aUSDT: `0x23878914EFE38d27C4D67Ab83ed1b93A74D4086a`
+
+Command:
+
+```bash
+forge test --match-contract UsdtYieldVaultMainnetForkTest -vvv
+```
+
