+Fix I would make: stop treating `totalAssetsStored` as the source of truth while funds sit in Aave. `totalAssets()` and conversion math should be based on actual custody, especially `aUsdt.balanceOf(address(this))`, because Aave yield accrues through the aToken balance. If withdrawal fees are meant to accrue to remaining shareholders, withdrawing user should receive `netAssets`, while the retained fee must remain part of remaining-shareholder assets. Also define the final-withdrawer case explicitly: either waive the fee when no shares remain, or send it to a real fee recipient instead of leaving it stranded inside the vault.
+
+## 3. High: owner can set deposit fee values that brick deposits
+
+`setDepositFee()` has no upper bound, and the constructor has no upper bound either. A fee at `10_000` bps is accepted, but every deposit reverts with `NoSharesMinted()` because the net amount is zero. Values above `10_000` bps are also accepted by the setter; later deposits revert from arithmetic underflow when computing `amount - fee`.
+
+How I found it: `test/UsdtYieldVaultFeeBounds.t.sol` fuzzes the accepted fee domain and checks the exact `10_000` bps boundary.
+
+Command:
+
+```bash
+forge test --match-contract UsdtYieldVaultFeeBoundsTest -vvv
